            <ArticleTitle>Vasospasm and myocardial bridge.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1440-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two cases are discussed where vasospasm was induced at the level of myocardial bridges in patients with a recent myocardial infarction. A review of the clinical significance of myocardial bridges is presented. It is hypothesized that myocardial bridges may predispose to vasospasm; therefore, testing for vasospasm in patients with otherwise normal coronary angiograms is suggested.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
